Spec folder: specs/cli-external-orchestration/082-opencode-v1-v2-dual-compat/040-dispatch-lint-held-fixes (pre-approved, skip Gate 3)

ROLE: Act as a code agent. Make one change to one function, `isUsableMention` in `.skilled/hooks/dispatch/pi/dispatch-preflight-lint.ts`, plus test rows.

Problem: every comma now starts a new clause, so `do not, under any circumstances, use cli-devin` authorizes cli-devin: the comma drops the `do not`. A comma must reset a negation only when it ends the negation's own clause, as in `not opencode, use cli-devin`.

Fix, replacing the clause logic in `isUsableMention` (keep the quote and expansion checks):
1. The sentence starts after the last newline, `;`, `.`, `!` or `?` before the mention, or after the last whole word `but`, `instead` or `rather` (case-insensitive) before the mention, whichever is later. Commas no longer start it.
2. In the text from the sentence start to the mention, find the LAST match of `NEGATION_PATTERN`. If there is none, the mention is not negated.
3. Otherwise the negation reaches the mention unless one of the commas between the negation and the mention closes the negation's clause. A comma closes it only when BOTH hold:
   a. the text from the end of the negation word to that comma names an executor: a `cli-` name, `/deep:`, or one of the words `opencode`, `claude`, `codex`, `devin`, `cursor`, `cursor-agent`, `pi`, `hermes`, `jev` (whole words, case-insensitive); and
   b. the text right after that comma, ignoring spaces, starts a new imperative: one of the whole words `use`, `run`, `try`, `pick`, `choose`, `call`, `dispatch`, `launch`, `prefer`, `switch`, `go` (case-insensitive).
   So a parenthetical (`do not, under any circumstances, use ...`) and a list (`do not use opencode, codex, or cli-devin`) keep the negation, while `not opencode, use cli-devin` and `never use codex, use cli-devin` end it.
Put the executor words and the imperative words in two named constants near `NEGATION_PATTERN`. Update the function's comment so it says this, briefly.

Tests: in `.skilled/hooks/dispatch/pi/dispatch-preflight-lint.test.ts`, add these rows to the `Pi dispatch deny matrix` table, after the row 'negation in the same clause as a deep-loop executor' (command `devin -p "task"` in every row; last value is whether it is denied):
